# interplay_memlive_self_mapped_table: A task whose VA page 20 is its own page-table page, as a shared buffer T. It reads its table through T, then writes its own leaf for VA page 12 with a GPU copy (buffer B, never made, is then made over the new page); then writes the leaf of page 20 itself, pointing T's VA at another page. T, live, still reads the table page (its copy of entry 20 shows the new leaf). Discarded (63) and listed with invalidateHost, T is made again over the table as it is now: the other page in the map setup and in the service; in the blocks setup the host task keeps the table page mapped at that VA.
